{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"buoyancy driven thermal flow buoyancy driven thermal flow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","fileName":"Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"buoyancy driven thermal flow buoyancy driven thermal flow","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","fileName":"Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow","heading":"Buoyancy-Driven Thermal Flow","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Heating changes fluid density, and gravity then produces a body force that can drive circulation. Warmer, less dense fluid rises while cooler, denser fluid descends, transporting energy in addition to molecular conduction.\n\nThis natural-convection feedback appears in a cup or kettle even without an imposed inlet velocity. A coupled model needs gravity, a consistent density law, and suitable walls or free surfaces to resolve the circulation rather than replacing it with a fixed [[Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient|boundary coefficient]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conjugate Heat Transfer Systems","Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","cosmolheattransfermodels